    "verdict": "REQUEST CHANGES",
    "findings": [
      {
        "id": "CR6-1",
        "class": "statement-contradiction",
        "severity": "HIGH",
        "title": "T2 omits `cmd/mcp-bridge/config_envelope_test.go`, which pins `len(EnvelopeFieldNames())==129` and sortedness (`:168-172`). `quarantine_path` makes 130, and insertion \"after `protocol_version`\" (`envelope.go:667`; next entry is `publication_impact`) is unsorted, so T3's full-suite gate cannot pass inside the §6.1 envelope. Fix: add that file to T2/§6.1, set 130, and insert after `publication_impact` in `envelope.go`, the docs union, and the `log_test.go` literal.",
        "anchor": "cmd/mcp-bridge/config_envelope_test.go",
        "fix": "add that file to T2/§6.1, set 130, and insert after `publication_impact` in `envelope.go`, the docs union, and the `log_test.go` literal."
      },
      {
        "id": "CR6-2",
        "class": "statement-contradiction",
        "severity": "HIGH",
        "title": "Double `startup_failed`. §4/T2 call `writeStartupFailure(stderr, stateDirectoryFailure(store.Dir()))` in serve and return the error; `runContext` also writes every returned error (`main.go:59-68`). AC2-4/AC2-7 \"one record\" therefore fails: duplicate `state_directory`, or `state_directory` plus fallback `internal_error` when the raw fatal is returned. Fix: serve emits accumulated warnings only and returns `stateDirectoryFailure(store.Dir())`; main remains the sole writer.",
        "anchor": "startup_failed",
        "fix": "serve emits accumulated warnings only and returns `stateDirectoryFailure(store.Dir())`; main remains the sole writer."
      },
      {
        "id": "CR6-3",
        "class": "statement-contradiction",
        "severity": "HIGH",
        "title": "Prune off-by-one. §4 step 4 excludes this run's file, then unlinks beyond `QuarantineKeep` among the remainder, leaving 6 when 5 pre-exist. R5 (≤5 per family) and AC1-3/AC1-9 require 5 survivors with the oldest removed. Fix: unlink beyond `QuarantineKeep-1` after exclusion.",
        "anchor": "QuarantineKeep",
        "fix": "unlink beyond `QuarantineKeep-1` after exclusion."
      },
      {
        "id": "CR6-4",
        "class": "statement-contradiction",
        "severity": "MEDIUM",
        "title": "§4 step 3 records the `Recovery` only after `syncDirectory` succeeds, but AC2-8(a) requires the result to carry it on a post-rename sync fatal, and R4 requires one warning per quarantined file. Fix: append the Recovery immediately after rename success, before sync.",
        "anchor": "Recovery",
        "fix": "append the Recovery immediately after rename success, before sync."
      },
      {
        "id": "CR6-5",
        "class": "ac-not-falsifiable",
        "severity": "MEDIUM",
        "title": "AC1-8's \"offset form\" `prompts.corrupt-20261121T120000+02:00.json` is not RFC3339 either (missing separators), so plain `time.Parse` also treats it as foreign; the literal-`Z` rule is unpinned. Fix: `prompts.corrupt-2026-11-21T12:00:00+02:00.json`.",
        "anchor": "prompts.corrupt-20261121T120000+02:00.json",
        "fix": "`prompts.corrupt-2026-11-21T12:00:00+02:00.json`."
      },
      {
        "id": "CR6-6",
        "class": "ac-not-falsifiable",
        "severity": "LOW",
        "title": "AC2-9's \"next prompt save\" has no named trigger; startup admission skips `PersistPrompts` (`reload.go:728`), leaving only the async initial refresh (`loop.go:172`). Name/poll it or assert persistence at service level.",
        "anchor": "PersistPrompts",
        "fix": ""
      },
      {
        "id": "CR6-7",
        "class": "editorial",
        "severity": "LOW",
        "title": "§9 risk(4) says the retained AC2-6 record \"collapses to `logging_write_failed`\"; §3 correctly shows wiring.go:485-492 writes via `observe.WriteJSONLine`, not `buildEnvelope`. Correct the note.",
        "anchor": "logging_write_failed",
        "fix": ""
      },
      {
        "id": "CR6-8",
        "class": "editorial",
        "severity": "LOW",
        "title": "Ticket example `snapshot.corrupt-20261116T230448Z.json` is not RFC3339Nano-`Z` under R5 and would never be pruned; stale and misleading.",
        "anchor": "snapshot.corrupt-20261116T230448Z.json",
        "fix": ""
      },
      {
        "id": "CR6-9",
        "class": "r-ac-coverage-gap",
        "severity": "LOW",
        "title": "R8's \"any other value enables recovery\" is untested; AC2-6 covers only `off`/`OFF`. Add one `enabled`/`1` case.",
        "anchor": "off",
        "fix": ""
      },
      {
        "id": "CR6-10",
        "class": "ac-not-falsifiable",
        "severity": "LOW",
        "title": "AC1-1's absent subcase \"performs no retention pass\" is unobservable unless >`QuarantineKeep` conforming files are seeded; seed and assert unchanged, or drop the clause.",
        "anchor": "QuarantineKeep",
        "fix": ""
      }
    ],
